    },
    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Successful exploitation of these vulnerabilities could allow an attacker to remotely send specially formatted UDP requests or connect to an unknown external network that would allow them to write arbitrary data, resulting in remote code execution. The device may also leak patient information and sensor data to the same unknown external network. Simultaneous exploitation of all vulnerable devices on a shared network is possible.",
        "title": "Risk evaluation"
      },
      {
        "category": "other",
        "text": "Healthcare and Public Health",
        "title": "Critical infrastructure sectors"
      },
      {
        "category": "general",
        "text": "CISA recommends users take defensive measures to minimize the risk of exploitation of these vulnerabilities, such as:",
        "title": "Recommended Practices"
      }
    ],
